Third-party components vendored into this repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following are copied verbatim from their published npm packages (unmodified
except for import-path patching) into `src/vendor/`. They are NOT covered by
this repository's Apache-2.0 licence; each retains its own MIT licence, and the
upstream licence text is preserved alongside the code.

1. @noble/curves 1.9.7 — https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-curves
   MIT License, Copyright (c) 2022 Paul Miller (https://paulmillr.com)
   Location: src/vendor/curves/  (licence: src/vendor/curves/LICENSE)
   Files: ed25519.js, utils.js,
          abstract/{curve,edwards,hash-to-curve,modular,montgomery}.js

2. @noble/hashes 1.8.0 — https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-hashes
   MIT License, Copyright (c) 2022 Paul Miller (https://paulmillr.com)
   Location: src/vendor/hashes/  (licence: src/vendor/hashes/LICENSE)
   Files: sha2.js, utils.js, _md.js, _u64.js, crypto.js

Why they are vendored rather than imported: `actor-host.js` wires Ed25519
`gen_keypair`/`sign`/`verify` as synchronous WASM host imports, and Web Crypto's
SubtleCrypto is async-only. Elliptic-curve arithmetic is not something to
hand-roll, so an audited implementation is copied in. A CDN `https:` import
specifier works in browsers but Node's default ESM loader rejects it outright,
which would break this project's own tests — hence file-for-file vendoring.
See `src/vendor/README.md` for the full rationale.

